2026-10-19T19:49:56.3631351Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3641505Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3749198Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3761122Z [0m
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3761779Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3762604Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3762993Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3763773Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3764952Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3765456Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3765785Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3766474Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3766795Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3767384Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3768340Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3769207Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3769842Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3770425Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3770725Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3771290Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3771649Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3772344Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3772624Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3772849Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3773155Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3773725Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3774590Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3775422Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3775874Z I will:
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3776372Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3776808Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3777604Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3778502Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3779362Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3780014Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3780644Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3781528Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3782312Z    /root
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3790561Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3791641Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3802833Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3804059Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3804968Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3805568Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3806597Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3825997Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3826630Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3840737Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3841617Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3842697Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3843328Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3843883Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3844971Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3845747Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3846566Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3846964Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3847163Z If you would like to
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3847668Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3847994Z 
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3848330Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-19T19:49:56.3849035Z   $ sh ./install-nix
